http://schema.org/contentRating currently expects text like "MPAA PG-13". Many authors simply provide the rating (e.g. "PG-13") and omit the rating organization.

It would be helpful to include in the range a ContentRatingScore with properties:
- contentRatingOrganization
- contentRating

It would make clear how to separate the rating organization and would allow for markup like:

```
{
  "@context": "http://schema.org",
  "@type": "Movie",
  "name":  "Ghostbusters",
  "contentRating": [
    {
      "@type": "ContentRatingScore",
      "contentRatingOrganization": {
         "@type": "Organization",
         "name": "MPAA",
      },
      "contentRating": "PG",
    },
    {
      "@type": "ContentRatingScore",
      "contentRatingOrganization": {
         "@type": "Organization",
         "name": "BBFC",
      },
      "contentRating": "PG",
    },
    {
      "@type": "ContentRatingScore",
      "contentRatingOrganization": {
         "@type": "Organization",
         "name": "France Ministry of Culture",
      },
      "contentRating": "U",
    },
  ]
}
```

Sites like Wikipedia and IMDB often provide the country of origin for TV series and movies. It would be nice if they had a way to do that in markup as well. Something like:

```
{
  "@context": "http://schema.org/",
  "@type": "Movie",
  "name": "Ghostbusters",
  "countryOfOrigin": {
    "@type": "Country",
    "name": "USA"
  }
}

```

In some cases, there will be more than one country, which is fine. Authors can provide more than one value.

