For data-sets and electronic documents, there is currently no way to specify a `Download` action, i.e. the fact of retrieving of data.
Why we need an attribute as opposed to just use the URL attribute:

* There might be different end-points, for different data representations, different protocols, or data variations (language).
* The download might be a complex or expensive action 

Example application

```
{
  "@context":  "https://schema.org/",
  "@type": "Product"
  "subjectOf": {
    "@type": "Official Document",
    "potentialAction": {
      "@type": "DownloadAction",
      "target": [
        {
          "@type": "EntryPoint",
          "contentType": "application/ld+json",
          "httpMethod": "GET"
          "url": "https://www.example.org/API-endpoint_as_JSON_LD"
        },
        {
          "@type": "EntryPoint",
          "contentType": "application/XML",
          "httpMethod": "GET"
          "url": "https://www.example.org/API-endpoint_as_XML"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

